media: imx: capture: allow vb2 cache hints (non-coherent MMAP buffers)

ForgeFIRM camera stream path. The i.MX6 has no hardware demosaic, so
userspace must read every captured Bayer frame. The default coherent MMAP
buffers map uncached on ARM, and CPU reads from an uncached mapping cost a
bus transaction per access - an order of magnitude slower than reading the
same DRAM through the cache. vb2 already implements the fix
(V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT REQBUFS allocates CPU-cached buffers and
does the cache maintenance at QBUF/DQBUF) but only when the driver opts in
via allow_cache_hints; opt the imx capture queue in. Userspace that does
not pass the flag is unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Scott Wiederhold <s.e.wiederhold@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx-media-capture.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx-media-capture.c
@@ -1025,7 +1025,15 @@
 	vq->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_MONOTONIC;
 	vq->lock = &priv->mutex;
 	vq->min_queued_buffers = 2;
 	vq->dev = priv->dev;
+	/*
+	 * ForgeFIRM: permit V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT (CPU-cached) MMAP
+	 * buffers. There is no hardware demosaic, so userspace reads every
+	 * captured Bayer frame; a cached mapping (vb2 does the cache
+	 * maintenance at QBUF/DQBUF) reads an order of magnitude faster than
+	 * the coherent uncached default.
+	 */
+	vq->allow_cache_hints = 1;
 
 	ret = vb2_queue_init(vq);
 	if (ret) {
